\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {(a)} Count-degradation curves. Error bars: $\pm 1$ standard deviation (SD) across 3 batch-composition seeds $\times $ 25 batches. RE declines monotonically; NER shows a U-shape. Rightmost points are full-schema (negligible sampling variance). \textbf  {(b)} Illustrative BCS-controlled FewRel accuracy: each bar represents one extreme-BCS batch per condition. Slopes are consistent across pool conditions ($p = 0.60$); wider BCS range at 80 relations produces larger gaps. Statistical evidence is provided by the pooled regression (\S  \ref {sec:bcs_controlled}, semipartial $R^2 = 0.273$, $n = 204$).}}{4}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:main_results}{{3}{4}{\textbf {(a)} Count-degradation curves. Error bars: $\pm 1$ standard deviation (SD) across 3 batch-composition seeds $\times $ 25 batches. RE declines monotonically; NER shows a U-shape. Rightmost points are full-schema (negligible sampling variance). \textbf {(b)} Illustrative BCS-controlled FewRel accuracy: each bar represents one extreme-BCS batch per condition. Slopes are consistent across pool conditions ($p = 0.60$); wider BCS range at 80 relations produces larger gaps. Statistical evidence is provided by the pooled regression (\S \ref {sec:bcs_controlled}, semipartial $R^2 = 0.273$, $n = 204$)}{figure.caption.8}{}}
