\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {32}{\ignorespaces BCS--F1 correlation under progressively relaxed NER matching. Relaxed span credits a match if the predicted span overlaps the gold span and the type is correct; token overlap uses token-level intersection; type-ignored drops the type constraint entirely. Relaxed matching improves mean F1 by 4.2\,pp (98.4\% of batches improve), but Pearson $r$ remains near zero across all modes (bootstrap 95\% CI crosses zero in all cases). Boundary errors affect all batches uniformly and do not mask a BCS signal.}}{26}{table.caption.86}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:relaxed_matching}{{32}{26}{BCS--F1 correlation under progressively relaxed NER matching. Relaxed span credits a match if the predicted span overlaps the gold span and the type is correct; token overlap uses token-level intersection; type-ignored drops the type constraint entirely. Relaxed matching improves mean F1 by 4.2\,pp (98.4\% of batches improve), but Pearson $r$ remains near zero across all modes (bootstrap 95\% CI crosses zero in all cases). Boundary errors affect all batches uniformly and do not mask a BCS signal}{table.caption.86}{}}
